        "content": "<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"k\">#check</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">1</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">...</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">3</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">|&gt;.</span><span class=\"n\">toList</span>\n<span class=\"c1\">-- parses as 1 ... (3 |&gt;.toList); error</span>\n<span class=\"k\">#check</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">1</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">+</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">2</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">...</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">3</span>\n<span class=\"c1\">-- parses as 1 + (2 ... 3); error</span>\n<span class=\"kd\">def</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">f</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">IO</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Unit</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">do</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"k\">let</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">List</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">Fin</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">10</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">*...*.</span><span class=\"n\">toList</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"c1\">-- inference works fine</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">for</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">i</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Fin</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">10</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">in</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">*...*</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">do</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">IO.println</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">i</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"c1\">-- error: typeclass instance problem is stuck</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"c1\">-- ForIn IO (Std.Rii ?m.3) (Fin 10)</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>The first two are parsing issues, each of which has one \"obviously correct\" parse. The first was reported in <a href=\"https://github.com/leanprover/lean4/pull/12055\">leanprover/lean4#12055</a>, and I constantly get hit by the second whenever I try to do something like <code>(x+1)...end</code> (though in this particular case I can get around it with left-exclusive ranges).</p>\n<p>The last one is an inference problem with the full range. Unlike other ranges, there's no information (the boundary values) for <code>*...*</code> to infer its intended type. The context is enough in some cases, but not in others; notably the <code>for ... in</code> breaks, and I couldn't find any alternative other than writing out the type like <code>*...* : Std.Rii (Fin 10)</code>.</p>",
